WEBVTT

00:26.110 --> 00:28.120
I beg you! Save me!

00:29.790 --> 00:30.740
Listen to me!

00:35.130 --> 00:37.040
Please, save me!

00:52.520 --> 00:53.650
This is the woman!

00:54.110 --> 00:55.230
Master Clerk!

00:56.740 --> 00:58.240
Please, wait!

00:58.780 --> 01:00.910
I... I've done nothing!

01:05.410 --> 01:07.210
Take her to the cape!

01:07.290 --> 01:10.040
No!!!

01:10.590 --> 01:13.340
Please, I want an investigation! An investigation!

01:29.330 --> 01:38.100
(Wanting you to just be near,
to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:38.140 --> 01:47.140
(Wishing you would call my name,
'Cause only you can light the flame)

01:47.180 --> 01:53.910
Constantly searching,
still can't find

01:56.520 --> 02:02.590
Ever illusive peace of mind

02:04.760 --> 02:13.330
Sometimes it's near,
but slips away

02:13.370 --> 02:19.970
And I'm faced with another day

02:21.180 --> 02:26.910
Of wanting you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

02:26.950 --> 02:31.250
...to just be near
('Cause only you can light the flame)

02:31.290 --> 02:35.730
Of wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

02:35.760 --> 02:40.160
...would call my name,
to feel your breath upon my ear

02:40.200 --> 02:44.690
Of wanting you... wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

02:44.740 --> 02:52.580
Call my name, 'cause only
you can light the flame

02:57.830 --> 02:57.860
Shinigami, or rather, the Shichinin Misaki: Part I

03:27.310 --> 03:30.520
Hear me! The rampant
kidnapping that has besieged our city

03:30.680 --> 03:34.560
was carried out by none other
than spies who seek to ruin our province!

03:34.900 --> 03:39.570
We will forgive none who
protect or aid these plotting criminals!

03:39.820 --> 03:43.490
We shall find them all and
attack this disaster at its source!

03:44.540 --> 03:45.490
Hey, look!

03:47.210 --> 03:49.870
We've burned seven of them!

03:50.250 --> 03:50.960
Seven...

03:52.460 --> 03:54.050
It must be... the Shichinin Misaki...

03:54.380 --> 03:56.590
The curse of the Shichinin Misaki!

04:05.730 --> 04:07.730
We can see the sea.

04:07.980 --> 04:10.730
We're neranng Kitabayashi province.

04:12.150 --> 04:15.410
Hey, Ogin!

04:15.490 --> 04:18.490
Sensei isn't following us.

04:19.540 --> 04:20.250
I know.

04:21.080 --> 04:24.290
We live in different worlds, sensei.

04:24.750 --> 04:26.380
Then let's live in the same--

04:26.590 --> 04:27.250
Stop it!

04:28.300 --> 04:32.050
There is a line that cannot be
crossed between human beings.

04:32.930 --> 04:38.020
Sensei... you're someone who must not enter this world...

04:39.190 --> 04:40.100
ever.

04:57.880 --> 04:59.290
I've never seen them before.

04:59.880 --> 05:01.130
From the looks of it...

05:01.210 --> 05:02.300
They are trying to silence us...

05:03.720 --> 05:05.140
Then, sensei must also be--

05:05.390 --> 05:12.440
[Note: Shinigami refers to the deity, Death.]

05:05.390 --> 05:08.640
He has also seen the Shinigami.

05:08.930 --> 05:12.440
And now that he has seen it, he must
make do with his own luck and survive.

05:14.360 --> 05:18.740
Then this Shinigami is in Kitabayashi right now?

05:26.040 --> 05:29.170
Kyougokutei, just what are you trying to do?

05:55.200 --> 05:56.620
Caught between two worlds...

05:56.870 --> 06:00.410
In the end, no matter where I go,
I'm still caught between two worlds.

06:06.130 --> 06:06.960
Hey, darling.

06:07.300 --> 06:10.720
The customer on the second
floor is going to hang himself for sure.

06:10.800 --> 06:12.140
You think so, too?

06:12.890 --> 06:15.930
Darling, how many years do
you think we've been in this business?

06:16.060 --> 06:19.940
Actually, the first time I met him, I knew for sure that...

06:20.020 --> 06:22.940
Shut up and get him out of
here before he brings us bad luck!

06:23.190 --> 06:26.450
Tell him he can die if he wants, but not to do it here!

06:26.860 --> 06:28.610
M-Me?

06:28.700 --> 06:29.120
Excuse me.

06:33.750 --> 06:35.080
If I recall, you're...

06:35.960 --> 06:37.960
I apologize for my rudeness
towards you in Sanuki province.

06:38.340 --> 06:41.800
I am Shinonome Ukon a former
servant of the Kitabayashi family.

06:42.510 --> 06:43.720
Kitabayashi...?

06:43.970 --> 06:45.090
Does the name ring a bell?

06:45.550 --> 06:48.560
No, it's just that I've heard rumors
about the curse of the Shichinin Misaki.

06:48.770 --> 06:49.430
What sort of rumors?

06:50.310 --> 06:53.520
What I know is an old legend about a type of youkai,

06:54.110 --> 06:58.230
but I hear that the Shichinin Misaki was
originally a group of youkai in Tosa province.

06:58.650 --> 06:59.820
If you encountered them, you would die.

07:00.150 --> 07:03.490
In a sense, it was a kind of
Shinigami, and there were seven of them.

07:04.120 --> 07:08.370
Each one would possess and kill seven;
so seven times seven and 49 would die.

07:08.830 --> 07:11.840
Then those 49 victims would each possess and kill
seven, so the number of vengeful spirits would not end,

07:12.300 --> 07:16.300
and would continue to increase like a pyramid scheme.

07:17.260 --> 07:20.680
Indeed. That's what happened in Kitabayashi province.

07:20.810 --> 07:21.470
What?!

07:22.060 --> 07:27.270
In the first year, seven
suddenly vanished from the castle town.

07:27.270 --> 07:31.820
In the year after, there
were 14, and the year after that, 28...

07:31.820 --> 07:34.820
and now a vast number of people have vanished.

07:35.570 --> 07:38.080
The fears of the populace has reached an extreme.

07:38.080 --> 07:39.870
They suspect everyone and everything,

07:39.870 --> 07:42.790
saying that this is the doing of
spies who have snuck into the province,

07:43.000 --> 07:45.340
and that someone must be supporting them.

08:04.190 --> 08:05.360
Has it gotten that bad?

08:08.320 --> 08:12.200
But... with so many people missing,
shouldn't there be some cities as to who is behind this?

08:13.620 --> 08:15.870
Even though the authorities
have conducted an extensive search,

08:16.210 --> 08:18.330
and have taken the strictest security precautions,

08:18.710 --> 08:21.300
there are no clues, and people continue to disappear.

08:21.760 --> 08:24.760
I, myself, am wondering if it really is a curse.

08:25.050 --> 08:26.510
The curse of the Shichinin Misaki?

08:26.970 --> 08:31.680
However, even if I were to believe that
this is all a conspiracy to ruin the province,

08:32.100 --> 08:34.190
that is still the only conclusion I can draw.

08:34.730 --> 08:38.360
I eventually found the situation
unbearable and left the province.

08:38.740 --> 08:39.610
You've committed dappan...?!

08:38.740 --> 08:42.910
[Note: Dappan refers to a samurai's withdrawal from
the provincial registry and becoming a ronin.]

08:40.360 --> 08:41.860
But, if you did that..!

08:41.910 --> 08:42.910
There was no other way.

08:43.990 --> 08:45.790
My wife also disappeared!

08:47.460 --> 08:48.410
She was pregnant...

08:49.210 --> 08:50.210
already three months heavy with a child.

08:50.880 --> 08:51.630
Pregnant...

08:52.340 --> 08:55.670
During the investigation, what we've
found from the spies' movements was...

08:55.880 --> 08:56.590
What was it?

08:57.260 --> 08:59.680
Yamaoka-dono, I saw it, too!

08:59.850 --> 09:01.310
That terrible weapon!

09:27.510 --> 09:28.800
There is suspicious activity involving it.

09:29.170 --> 09:30.880
Then the Hikasou has appeared again?

09:35.470 --> 09:38.480
Yamaoka-dono, you are in the jaws of death.

09:38.600 --> 09:40.480
The jaws of death? Me?

09:41.020 --> 09:43.270
You know something that must not be known!

09:53.160 --> 09:54.910
I'll be leaving for a while.

09:55.120 --> 09:57.080
That's unusual.

09:57.500 --> 09:59.170
What about that ronin samurai?

09:59.460 --> 10:01.050
He's still in my room.

10:08.680 --> 10:10.060
Come back soon--

10:10.100 --> 10:12.140
He's not coming back.

10:12.270 --> 10:13.600
I feel relieved.

10:13.980 --> 10:16.400
Well, may his soul find peace in the afterlife...

10:16.480 --> 10:19.030
Actually, I also thought that
he might not be coming back.

10:19.110 --> 10:21.030
Hey, what about the money for the room?

10:22.870 --> 10:24.240
Yup, I have everything he gave me.

10:31.590 --> 10:34.510
Within this crowd, there are
those who seek to take my life.

10:35.050 --> 10:37.550
How strange... I'm not scared at all.

10:38.090 --> 10:40.890
Could it be that my heart already longs for death?

10:41.140 --> 10:45.060
For someone who longs for death... isn't that
what it truly means to be in the jaws of death?

10:45.440 --> 10:47.480
Momosuke-san!

10:50.280 --> 10:51.190
Heihachi-san?

10:52.570 --> 10:53.320
I thought it was you.

10:53.740 --> 10:56.450
Heihachi-san, I'm sorry, but I really need to get going...

10:56.660 --> 10:57.160
Huh?

10:57.620 --> 11:00.580
Hey, what's wrong? You're in such a hurry.

11:00.790 --> 11:03.250
Youd better not get involved with me.

11:03.330 --> 11:07.630
What are you saying? It must be
some kind of fate that we're meeting here.

11:07.960 --> 11:10.170
Oh yeah, I need to tell you about
Kitabayashi province's castle town.

11:10.630 --> 11:11.680
Kitabayashi?!

11:13.260 --> 11:16.140
I've never been so scared in my entire life!

11:16.810 --> 11:19.980
I wonder if that's what it feels
like to walk into a den of wolves.

11:20.190 --> 11:23.820
If I hadn't been summoned directly by the castle,
who knows if I would've been able to return alive?

11:24.490 --> 11:25.900
I sure don't want to go
through the same experience ever again.

11:26.320 --> 11:27.860
Directly by the castle?

11:28.070 --> 11:30.320
What they were after was this.

11:31.580 --> 11:35.120
It seems there are curious people
out there at the end of the earth.

11:35.750 --> 11:38.670
[Note: Muzan'e was a woodblock print genre featuring various violent
acts that enjoyed subculture status during the Edo period.]

11:35.750 --> 11:37.500
It's called a Muzan'e.

11:41.970 --> 11:42.920
A pregnant woman...!

11:43.430 --> 11:47.720
Well, it's pretty risque stuff.
Established publishers won't touch it.

11:48.140 --> 11:51.810
Seven new ones are made
each year, and there are 28 in all.

11:52.020 --> 11:53.650
Seven, you say?

11:53.940 --> 11:55.820
Momosuke-san, what's wrong?

11:56.610 --> 11:57.650
Heihachi-san!

11:57.740 --> 11:59.990
Who did you sell this scroll to?

12:00.030 --> 12:03.570
L-Like I said, it was a direct summon from the castle.

12:04.830 --> 12:05.700
The castle...

12:08.160 --> 12:08.960
Momosuke-san!

12:09.000 --> 12:09.870
Ukon-san!

12:12.210 --> 12:16.090
No... it can't possibly be the curse of the Shichinin Misaki!

12:16.430 --> 12:18.890
If it is, then Mataichi-san and his group are...

12:39.900 --> 12:41.610
W-Wait!

12:42.450 --> 12:44.450
If it's about that, I'll never tell a soul!

12:44.930 --> 12:45.910
I...

12:46.740 --> 12:51.120
I... can't die...

12:51.380 --> 12:53.250
I just can't die, yet!

12:54.590 --> 12:58.090
I-It's not that I don't want to die... Please!

13:01.470 --> 13:02.810
Yamaoka-dono!

13:35.350 --> 13:37.430
You're faster than I thought you were.

13:37.520 --> 13:39.350
I fell behind. I'm sorry.

13:40.100 --> 13:42.100
These are men I saw in Sanuki.

13:42.690 --> 13:43.940
As I've thought, the Hikasou must be involved.

13:44.610 --> 13:51.570
Ukon-san... the Shichinin Misaki isn't a curse.

13:52.830 --> 13:56.210
The Shichinin Misaki is the doing of a human!

13:56.620 --> 13:58.210
How do you know that?

13:58.500 --> 14:02.050
The villain is probably in Kitabayashi's castle.

14:10.680 --> 14:12.520
We haven't gotten enough of them, yet!

14:13.230 --> 14:14.350
Listen, everyone!

14:14.770 --> 14:17.650
There are more of these dogs hiding in our lands!

14:18.030 --> 14:21.950
There's no need to hold back... find them all!

14:22.360 --> 14:25.030
This is hell on earth.

14:34.340 --> 14:36.670
What is this construction for?

14:48.100 --> 14:49.100
Yamaoka-dono!

14:49.980 --> 14:50.560
Yes?

14:50.610 --> 14:52.190
We can go no further on horseback.

14:53.280 --> 14:54.320
We'll have to go through a difficult route.

14:55.910 --> 14:57.320
D-Don't worry!

14:59.740 --> 15:01.450
Now I'm worried!

15:08.670 --> 15:10.510
I can see our destination, Yamaoka-dono!

15:13.010 --> 15:15.680
That's... Kitabayashis castle.

15:16.970 --> 15:19.390
It's all like a bad dream...

15:19.810 --> 15:23.190
The previous lady of the castle, Kaede no Kata-sama,

15:23.230 --> 15:24.320
leapt from that tower to her death...

15:41.590 --> 15:43.880
The strange disappearances in the castle town began then.

15:44.090 --> 15:46.890
After that, everything...

15:47.850 --> 15:50.680
We should wait until sundown before entering the town.

15:59.530 --> 16:00.240
That's...

16:00.780 --> 16:03.070
The master of the castle, Danjou-sama.

16:05.450 --> 16:06.440
Toranoshi...

16:07.750 --> 16:08.870
What have you done to your own mother?

16:13.920 --> 16:14.500
Denzou.

16:14.750 --> 16:15.050
Yes.

16:15.840 --> 16:16.710
When will it be done?

16:16.720 --> 16:18.260
It will take another month.

16:18.260 --> 16:19.430
You have half of that.

16:19.430 --> 16:21.090
We can wait no longer than that.

16:21.100 --> 16:22.050
Yes, sir!

16:27.850 --> 16:30.150
What are you trying to do, Mata no Ji?

16:30.520 --> 16:32.440
We're going to sneak into the castle!

16:32.820 --> 16:33.740
What did you say?

16:36.160 --> 16:37.110
Oh no!

16:40.830 --> 16:43.870
Those are some travelers that wandered into the province.

16:44.210 --> 16:45.210
This is bad.

16:57.980 --> 16:59.390
What are you doing, at this time of night?

16:59.560 --> 17:06.110
Sir, we have only barely reached the town. It took
more time to get through the pass than we expected.

17:06.650 --> 17:11.280
Oh? That must've been difficult!

17:19.000 --> 17:21.340
Hey, what do we do with this girl?

17:32.810 --> 17:33.810
Shiragiku!

17:38.280 --> 17:40.150
The deed is done!

17:41.900 --> 17:43.410
Mataichi-san!

17:48.790 --> 17:53.130
I... Shiragiku... will shine while remaining in darkness!

17:54.130 --> 17:57.010
As we've thought, she was involved.

18:01.100 --> 18:02.970
Take her with us, Kaburagi.

18:03.100 --> 18:03.510
Yes, ma'am!

18:10.900 --> 18:13.990
The curse of the Shichinin Misaki... It can't be...

18:15.150 --> 18:17.360
This is troublesome.

18:18.740 --> 18:19.830
Yamaoka-dono.

18:20.290 --> 18:20.870
Yes?

18:21.450 --> 18:26.420
My wife, Suzu... Could she really have
ended up like that person in the Muzan'e?

18:27.840 --> 18:30.050
It is only a speculation on my part...

18:30.800 --> 18:35.550
It's just that the person who was after the
Muzan'e scroll with seven drawings is in the castle...

18:35.760 --> 18:36.470
Seven drawings?

18:37.060 --> 18:38.680
Is that the Shichinin Misaki's...

18:38.770 --> 18:39.600
Ukon-san!

18:43.900 --> 18:44.690
That's...

18:54.500 --> 18:57.460
No... they're not going to do to
her what was done in those pictures...

19:05.510 --> 19:08.350
Kaburagi, it was you! You bastard!

19:10.140 --> 19:12.100
You came back, Ukon?

19:12.390 --> 19:15.560
Do you want to continue this
even tough your wife is alive?

19:15.610 --> 19:16.400
What did you say?!

19:16.940 --> 19:20.780
Since her pregnancy had yet to reach
full term, we decided to let her live till then!

19:20.820 --> 19:23.160
Then, as I've thought, you guys are--

19:23.570 --> 19:24.700
Stay your swords!

19:32.790 --> 19:35.500
What an idiot samurai.

19:36.590 --> 19:37.510
Ogin-san!

19:37.760 --> 19:38.720
Mataichi-san!

19:39.090 --> 19:43.470
You're quite the lucky one, sensei.

19:44.270 --> 19:46.980
Oh, we have some newcomers.

19:47.270 --> 19:48.650
Let's withdraw for now.

19:52.480 --> 19:54.490
I see. So they're reenacting the depicted scenes?

19:54.780 --> 19:57.030
Then, that scream we heard was...

19:57.200 --> 19:59.620
Then, sooner or later,
that girl will be used in a reenactment?

20:00.120 --> 20:04.250
With all that aside, I must say you've
thought of something quite horrible, sensei.

20:04.920 --> 20:05.630
That's...

20:06.790 --> 20:08.670
But in the end, Ukon-san was...

20:08.760 --> 20:11.170
Jeez, you're annoying.

20:11.630 --> 20:13.220
If that's so, then what would you do, huh?

20:13.340 --> 20:14.800
Well, I just...

20:14.850 --> 20:17.100
You've gotten him involved this far, and now this?

20:18.270 --> 20:19.100
Jeez...

20:21.600 --> 20:25.270
Sensei, there's nothing for you to feel bad about.

20:26.030 --> 20:28.950
That samurai was searching for a place to die.

20:29.240 --> 20:30.320
A place to die?

20:31.120 --> 20:34.330
Well now... shall we get started on the setup?

20:35.290 --> 20:35.750
Ogin.

20:37.000 --> 20:38.330
It's your turn.

20:52.690 --> 20:54.270
Th-That's...

20:56.650 --> 20:58.650
I am Lady Misaki.

20:59.940 --> 21:02.150
I am unable to carry out the vengeance I seek.

21:02.910 --> 21:06.620
If you wish to quell my curse, enshrine me!

21:07.540 --> 21:08.750
Enshrine me!

21:15.130 --> 21:16.510
What's with this castle?

21:17.420 --> 21:19.930
Secret doors, weird passages...

21:20.140 --> 21:23.180
Well, that made it easy to sneak in.

21:23.810 --> 21:26.060
This castle just seems suspicious to me.

21:26.850 --> 21:29.350
Don't you hear something?

21:49.800 --> 21:51.380
That's the Hikasou!

21:58.890 --> 22:00.560
We've found it.

22:00.940 --> 22:02.810
He is the Shinigami.

22:02.940 --> 22:05.980
And our opponent...

22:07.320 --> 22:10.490
the lord of the castle, Kitabayashi Danjou...

22:16.430 --> 22:22.520
Wind chimes whisper
soft and sweet

22:23.870 --> 22:29.960
Though there's not
a hint of a breeze

22:30.940 --> 22:36.710
Moonlight dancing
on the garden walk

22:36.750 --> 22:43.380
As it gently drifts
through the trees

22:44.750 --> 22:50.690
Romance takes flight
on this perfect night

22:50.730 --> 22:57.390
While all of the world
lays sleeping

22:58.230 --> 23:07.700
Find us here as we feel
the moment of love

23:09.010 --> 23:12.210
Draw near

23:12.480 --> 23:19.480
Dream, sleep,
with your hand in mine

23:19.520 --> 23:25.460
Underneath a blanket of stars

23:27.630 --> 23:32.900
Song birds singing
in a distant glade

23:32.940 --> 23:41.570
As we share
the warmth of the dawn

23:48.680 --> 23:53.900
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness.
All that remains is a dubious rumor among the townsfolk.

23:54.320 --> 23:56.860
Youkai, the darkness in people's hearts.

23:57.370 --> 23:59.410
There is as much sadness as there are demons.

24:00.010 --> 24:04.490
That is why I write this;
the sorrowful darkness of the ayakashi.

24:05.080 --> 24:08.170
On the next Kyougoku Natsuhiko's Rumors: 100 Stories,

24:08.540 --> 24:14.220
the final episode: Shinigami,
or rather, Shichinin Misaki: Part Two

24:14.830 --> 24:17.050
The deed is done.
